::kind(fixture)
// A quoted string before `:` is a map key, so a path or a URL can key an
// entry. It works in `{value}` groups and in `(args)` alike, because both
// read entries through the same value grammar as a standalone cotomet file.
::meta{
  "tmtroot/schema/rust.vocabulary.tmt": "../vocabularies/rust.vocabulary.tmt"
  "with space": 1
  plain.key: 2
}

=[ Quoted map keys ]

A key that is not an identifier is written as a quoted string.

@ns.thing("a/b.tmt": 1, plain: 2)

@ns.thing{ "a/b": { "c d": 3 } }

A quoted string with no `:` after it is still a value, not a key.

@ns.thing("a/b.tmt")
